 "brief": "# Approve/Deny in the console do nothing (URGENT, Brett Nov 7)\n\nBug: in the console's \"Approval waiting\" dialog (approvals-in-place, landed today on main), clicking Approve repeatedly does nothing; the dialog stays. It says \"This browser can't decide from here: its axHub session didn't reach the console. Use Open on axHub below.\" Brett is signed in to the console as owner (Admin).\n\n1. Make Approve/Deny work from the console with the console's own owner login: the console server relays the decision to axHub using a server-side owner credential (owner-only, audited), no separate axHub sign-in in the browser. Follow axHub's approvals API; coordinate with orchestrator-vps-gate if landed.\n2. While a decision is in flight: disable the button, show a spinner; on success close the dialog; on failure show the exact reason in place. Never a dead clickable button.\n3. Also fix in AmberX if it shares the dialog.\n4. Tests: approve, deny, expired, already decided, relay down. Screenshots to UI Review with three options (--choices). Add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push.",
